@facade = http://localhost:5122
@legacy = http://localhost:5240
@modern = http://localhost:5241
@alice = 10001
@bob = 10002

### The client only knows the facade. At the start (appsettings.json): the lookup is already migrated,
### the operations are in shadow mode, the statement and the transfers are still served by the legacy system.
### The X-Served-By header of each response tells who answered.
GET {{facade}}/accounts/{{alice}}

### Shadow mode: the legacy system answers, the modern one is called in parallel and compared (see /facade/comparisons)
GET {{facade}}/accounts/{{alice}}/operations

### Still served by the legacy system
GET {{facade}}/accounts/{{alice}}/statement

### Still served by the legacy system. The modern service catches up through its log (synchronization every 500 ms).
POST {{facade}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "{{alice}}", "target": "{{bob}}", "amount": 50 }

### A function nobody listed: it is not in the table, it goes to the legacy system
GET {{facade}}/branches

### The internal routes of both systems do not go through the facade (404)
GET {{facade}}/internal/log

# ─── Steering the migration (X-Admin-Key header) ───

### The routing table: the mode of each route, and how many calls each system served
GET {{facade}}/facade/routes
X-Admin-Key: demo

### The shadow mode comparisons: identical, divergences (with both bodies), abandoned (modern too slow)
GET {{facade}}/facade/comparisons
X-Admin-Key: demo

### Switch the transfers to the modern service, live
PUT {{facade}}/facade/routes/transfers
X-Admin-Key: demo
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mode": "Modern" }

### … the same call is now served by the modern service (X-Served-By: modern), which forwards it to the legacy system
POST {{facade}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "{{alice}}", "target": "{{bob}}", "amount": 25 }

### Rolling back is the same operation, the other way round: the legacy system already knows the 25 € transfer
PUT {{facade}}/facade/routes/transfers
X-Admin-Key: demo
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mode": "Legacy" }

### Refused: shadow mode would execute the transfer twice
PUT {{facade}}/facade/routes/transfers
X-Admin-Key: demo
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mode": "Shadow" }

### Where does the migration stand? "legacyRemovable" is only true if everything is migrated AND nothing calls the legacy system any more
GET {{facade}}/facade/progress
X-Admin-Key: demo

# ─── Behind the scenes (directly on both systems) ───

### The legacy system's night batch: it writes without going through the facade, the modern one catches up anyway
POST {{legacy}}/internal/fees
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ACCNUM": "{{alice}}", "AMTCTS": 250, "OPELBL": "Account maintenance fee" }

### The legacy change log, as the anti-corruption layer reads it (cents, six-letter columns)
GET {{legacy}}/internal/log?since=0

### The state of the modern service's synchronization: position in the log, operations still to forward
GET {{modern}}/internal/state
